# tools/notices/table: the linked crates tools/notices.sh cannot cover
# from their package. A crate whose package has no license file and
# whose expression offers no Apache-2.0 takes its row here, or the
# script refuses it by name. One row a crate, tab-separated:
#   name  version  source  sha256  holder
# source: <file>:<first>-<last>, those lines of a file of the package,
# or toolchain:<file>, a text of the toolchain's licenses/ folder
# (share/doc/rust/licenses/ of its sysroot). sha256: the text's, as the
# script cuts it; a different one refuses, so the row is read again.
# holder, optional: a copyright line written above the text, for a
# package that carries none; the notices then say that it carries none
# and that the holder is the author its manifest gives, the name
# without the address (ruled 2026-10-20).
#
# riscv, riscv-pac and riscv-rt are ISC, their notice the License
# section of their README; void is MIT, with no notice in its package
# (its README says "MIT").
